        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b486140695ff298cf04f1060b6593728cb49694efba73e3cbed60fae3a9ada75\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Assign all switch ports not in use to an inactive VLAN.\n\nStep 1: Assign the disabled interfaces to an inactive VLAN.\n\nSW1(config)# int e1/81-128\nSW1(config-if-range)# switchport access vlan 999\nSW1(config-if-range)# end\n\nStep 2: Configure trunk links to not allow traffic from the inactive VLAN.\n\nSW1(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan except 999\nSW1(config-if)# end",
          "group_id": "V-220690",
          "group_id_src": "V-220690",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000007",
          "rule_id": "SV-220690r991946_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220690r991946_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must have all disabled switch ports assigned to an unused VLAN.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000210",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "ac88c1be-1d0e-510f-b4c0-519c3e17f631",
          "uuid": "f14fab5d-c887-506f-b1ca-7fb2dea8f2dc",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b486140695ff298cf04f1060b6593728cb49694efba73e3cbed60fae3a9ada75\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Remove the assignment of the default VLAN from all access switch ports.",
          "group_id": "V-220691",
          "group_id_src": "V-220691",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000008",
          "rule_id": "SV-220691r991947_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220691r991947_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must not have the default VLAN assigned to any host-facing switch ports.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000220",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "ac88c1be-1d0e-510f-b4c0-519c3e17f631",
          "uuid": "14e1d6a9-878c-50c5-8247-648fbad1adbe",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b486140695ff298cf04f1060b6593728cb49694efba73e3cbed60fae3a9ada75\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Step 1: Prune VLAN 1 from any trunk links as necessary.\n\nSW1(config)# int e1/2\nSW1(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan except 1, 999\nSW1(config-if)# end\n\nStep 2: Verify VLAN 1 is not allowed on the trunk link.\n\nSW1# show interface trunk\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPort Native Status Port\n Vlan Channel\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEth1/1 1 trunking --\nEth1/2 1 trunking --\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPort Vlans Allowed on Trunk\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEth1/1 1-998,1000-4094\nEth1/2 2-998,1000-4094",
          "group_id": "V-220692",
          "group_id_src": "V-220692",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000009",
          "rule_id": "SV-220692r991948_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220692r991948_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must have the default VLAN pruned from all trunk ports that do not require it.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000230",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "ac88c1be-1d0e-510f-b4c0-519c3e17f631",
          "uuid": "81ffe25b-d613-5529-b675-dace85258176",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b486140695ff298cf04f1060b6593728cb49694efba73e3cbed60fae3a9ada75\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the switch for management access to use a VLAN other than the default VLAN.\n\nSW1(config)# interface vlan 44\nSW1(config-if)# ip add 10.1.12.1/24\nSW1(config-if)# end",
          "group_id": "V-220693",
          "group_id_src": "V-220693",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000010",
          "rule_id": "SV-220693r991949_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220693r991949_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must not use the default VLAN for management traffic.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000240",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "ac88c1be-1d0e-510f-b4c0-519c3e17f631",
          "uuid": "44e82332-c81c-50e4-954d-5ed854194a99",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b486140695ff298cf04f1060b6593728cb49694efba73e3cbed60fae3a9ada75\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Disable trunking on all user-facing or untrusted switch ports.\n\nSW1(config)# int e1/3-128\nSW1(config-if)# switchport mode access\nSW1(config-if)# end",
          "group_id": "V-220694",
          "group_id_src": "V-220694",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000011",
          "rule_id": "SV-220694r991951_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220694r991951_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must have all user-facing or untrusted ports configured as access switch ports.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000250",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "ac88c1be-1d0e-510f-b4c0-519c3e17f631",
          "uuid": "16c734bc-687f-5e48-92e5-b46a9295cb6d",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b486140695ff298cf04f1060b6593728cb49694efba73e3cbed60fae3a9ada75\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "To ensure the integrity of the trunk link and prevent unauthorized access, the ID of the native VLAN of the trunk port must be changed from the default VLAN (i.e., VLAN 1) to its own unique VLAN ID. \n\nSW1(config)#int e0/1\nSW1(config-if)#switchport trunk native vlan 44\n\nNote: The native VLAN ID must be the same on both ends of the trunk link; otherwise, traffic could accidentally leak between broadcast domains.",
          "group_id": "V-220695",
          "group_id_src": "V-220695",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000012",
          "rule_id": "SV-220695r991952_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220695r991952_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must have the native VLAN assigned to an ID other than the default VLAN for all 802.1q trunk links.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000260",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "ac88c1be-1d0e-510f-b4c0-519c3e17f631",
          "uuid": "f8bf0a33-e25d-5b89-9bc9-4684c92ea133",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b486140695ff298cf04f1060b6593728cb49694efba73e3cbed60fae3a9ada75\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure all access switch ports to a VLAN other than the native VLAN.",
